# DJ SPL Meter Project Documentation

## Project Overview
The DJ SPL Meter is an ESPHome-based sound pressure level meter with a graphical display. The main configuration file is [dj-spl-meter.yaml](mdc:hardware/db-dj-display/dj-spl-meter.yaml).

## Hardware Components
- ESP32-S3 DevKitC-1 board
- ST7701S-based 480x480 LCD display
- GT911 touchscreen controller
- External SPL sensor (connected via MQTT)

## Key Features
1. Real-time SPL monitoring with peak and average measurements
2. Configurable volume thresholds with visual indicators
3. WiFi connectivity with MQTT integration
4. Touch-enabled display interface
5. Time display synchronization

## Configuration Structure
The main configuration file is organized into these sections:
1. Core ESPHome configuration
2. Network and API settings (WiFi, MQTT, API)
3. Sensor configurations
4. Display and UI components
5. Hardware interfaces (I2C, SPI)

## User Interface
The display shows:
- Current SPL value in large digits
- Average SPL over 1-minute window
- Peak SPL measurements
- Visual status indicators
- Time display
- WiFi connection status

## Volume Thresholds
Three configurable thresholds with corresponding visual indicators:
- Low: Default 80 dB (Green)
- Medium: Default 90 dB (Yellow)
- High: Default 96 dB (Red)

## Dependencies
- ESPHome framework
- ESP-IDF
- LVGL for graphics
- External MQTT broker for SPL data

## Notes
- The project uses PSRAM for enhanced memory capabilities
- Secrets are stored in [secrets.yaml](mdc:hardware/db-dj-display/secrets.yaml)
- Display updates are optimized for performance
